        "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
        "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued October 29 at 1:21PM PDT until October 30 at 2:00PM PDT by NWS San Diego CA",
        "description": "* WHAT...Minor coastal flooding.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas and Orange County\nCoastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...For the Coastal Flood Advisory, from 1 PM today to 2 PM\nPDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of lots, parks, and roads with only\nisolated road closures expected.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Coastal residents and managers of\ninfrastructure in the advisory area should prepare for rising\nwater and take appropriate action to protect life and property.\nHighest tides will occur around noon on Friday. Observed high\ntides are 1.3 to 1.6 feet above astronomical tide predictions.",
        "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.",
